   1:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c **** /**
   2:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * @file
   3:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * Transmission Control Protocol, outgoing traffic
   4:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *
   5:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * The output functions of TCP.
   6:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *
   7:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * There are two distinct ways for TCP segments to get sent:
   8:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * - queued data: these are segments transferring data or segments containing
   9:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   SYN or FIN (which both count as one sequence number). They are created as
  10:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   struct @ref pbuf together with a struct tcp_seg and enqueue to the
  11:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   unsent list of the pcb. They are sent by tcp_output:
  12:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - @ref tcp_write : creates data segments
  13:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - @ref tcp_split_unsent_seg : splits a data segment
  14:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - @ref tcp_enqueue_flags : creates SYN-only or FIN-only segments
  15:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - @ref tcp_output / tcp_output_segment : finalize the tcp header
  16:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *      (e.g. sequence numbers, options, checksum) and output to IP
  17:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - the various tcp_rexmit functions shuffle around segments between the
  18:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *     unsent an unacked lists to retransmit them
  19:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - tcp_create_segment and tcp_pbuf_prealloc allocate pbuf and
  20:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *     segment for these functions
  21:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * - direct send: these segments don't contain data but control the connection
  22:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   behaviour. They are created as pbuf only and sent directly without
  23:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   enqueueing them:
  24:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - @ref tcp_send_empty_ack sends an ACK-only segment
  25:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - @ref tcp_rst sends a RST segment
  26:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - @ref tcp_keepalive sends a keepalive segment
  27:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - @ref tcp_zero_window_probe sends a window probe segment
  28:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *   - tcp_output_alloc_header allocates a header-only pbuf for these functions
  29:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  */
  30:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c **** 
