1958:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c **** /**
1959:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * Send a TCP RESET packet (empty segment with RST flag set) either to
1960:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * abort a connection or to show that there is no matching local connection
1961:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * for a received segment.
1962:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *
1963:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * Called by tcp_abort() (to abort a local connection), tcp_input() (if no
1964:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * matching local pcb was found), tcp_listen_input() (if incoming segment
1965:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * has ACK flag set) and tcp_process() (received segment in the wrong state)
1966:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *
1967:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * Since a RST segment is in most cases not sent for an active connection,
1968:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * tcp_rst() has a number of arguments that are taken from a tcp_pcb for
1969:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * most other segment output functions.
1970:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  *
1971:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * @param pcb TCP pcb (may be NULL if no pcb is available)
1972:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * @param seqno the sequence number to use for the outgoing segment
1973:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * @param ackno the acknowledge number to use for the outgoing segment
1974:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * @param local_ip the local IP address to send the segment from
1975:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * @param remote_ip the remote IP address to send the segment to
1976:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * @param local_port the local TCP port to send the segment from
1977:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  * @param remote_port the remote TCP port to send the segment to
1978:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_out.c ****  */
